<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="77272" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE/406/77272.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="ECE" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE.xml">Electrical and Computer Engineering</subject><course id="406" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/ECE/406.xml">Quantum Optics and Devices</course></parents><sectionNumber>QO </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course prepares ECE students with the essential quantum physics and device knowledge for the advent of quantum technology. The first half of the course will cover concepts and formalisms developed in quantum optics, which are widely used for analysis of various quantum devices and systems. The second half of the course will be focused on the application of the theoretical tools to study different quantum device platforms.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>09:00 AM</start><end>09:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2015</roomNumber><buildingName>Electrical &amp; Computer Eng Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Fang" firstName="K">Fang, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>